Subject: [PATCH 4/4] dense_cam_poses: the last pose keeps a command, so the command list is as long as the poses

Crash fix. dense_cam_poses densifies the route's camera poses and copies each segment's command
onto the poses it adds, but appends the final pose without its command, so after it the command
list is one entry shorter than the pose list. _get_info looks up commands[nearest_cam_idx]; when
the ego is nearest the route's last pose, that index is one past the end -- IndexError in the
simulator, and the episode dies with no score (hug_sim.py _get_info, kitti360
scene-3000_3200-easy-00 with SimLingo: both attempts, after it drove to the route's end).

Fix: the last pose takes the last command. Every pose and every earlier command is unchanged
(checked on all 82 released scenes), and _get_info is the only reader of the list, so an episode
that never reaches the last pose is unchanged.

Not reachable from outside: the crash is inside the simulator. Upstreamable.

diff --git a/sim/utils/sim_utils.py b/sim/utils/sim_utils.py
--- a/sim/utils/sim_utils.py
+++ b/sim/utils/sim_utils.py
@@ -91,6 +91,8 @@
                 dense_poses.append(interp_pose)
                 dense_cmds.append(cmds[i])
         dense_poses.append(cam_poses[-1])
+        # The last pose takes the last command too, so commands[i] is defined for every pose.
+        dense_cmds.append(cmds[-1])
         dense_poses = np.stack(dense_poses)
         cam_poses = dense_poses
         cmds = dense_cmds
